rules_version = '2';

// RIPSY commerce database: ripsy-commerce (Enterprise Native, europe-west3).
// Assumed backend-only model, scoped to commerce/{namespace}/:
// - settings/{prices|pack|registry|draft|migration}: structured payload maps for
//   catalog registrations, revisions, exact prices/currencies and bounded audit
//   history; one metadata-only draft; and a verified migration/cutover marker.
// - shopOrders/{id}, packOrders/{id}: immutable order IDs and structured receipt
//   payload maps (player/buyer identities, exact quotes/transactions/signatures,
//   statuses and private recovery/paid-entitlement state), plus recovery/lease
//   metadata. Paid receipts must not be discarded by a client.
// - leases/{id}: backend transaction fencing tokens and expiry metadata.
// Client schema assumptions cannot grant access: all names, IDs, fields, types,
// sizes and ownership values are denied, including future schema versions.
// Binary Rive/PNG/generated metadata files belong in private Cloud Storage,
// never in Firestore documents.
//
// There are deliberately NO direct mobile/web Firestore queries or writes.
// Existing HTTP session, buyer-wallet and admin-wallet checks remain on the
// backend. A Firebase sign-in or custom admin claim grants no database access.
// Public catalog responses are projected through the backend, not this Rules
// layer: a public figure must never make an order or private draft readable.
//
// Admin/server SDKs bypass Security Rules. The runtime service account therefore
// needs narrowly scoped IAM, and backend code must validate every create/update,
// preserve ownership/quotes and fence retries itself. Client domain validators
// or ownership helpers would not protect those server writes; no client payload
// is permitted here. This recursive fallback also denies unknown collections,
// collection-group queries and orphaned/nested subcollections.
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
